3. Connect Local Repo to GitHub Branch
----------------------------------------
# Step 1: Initialize git (skip if already a git repo)
git init

# Step 2: Add remote origin (skip if already added)
git remote add origin https://github.com/Goutham-Kumar-Nalumasu/Property_and_Home_Insurance_AI_Copilot_01.git

# Step 3: Fetch all branches from remote
git fetch origin

# Step 4: Switch to the develop branch
git checkout develop
# OR if branch doesn't exist locally yet:
git checkout -b develop origin/develop


4. Stage, Commit & Push
-----------------------
# Stage all files (respects .gitignore automatically)
git add .

# Verify what's being staged — confirm .env is NOT listed
git status

# Commit your changes
git commit -m "your commit message here"

# Push to develop branch
git push origin develop






if you see .env is not ignored  use 
-----------------------
git rm --cached .env
git rm --cached new-key.txt
git commit -m "remove sensitive files from tracking"
git push origin develop
